<------------------> example 2: <---------------->
//Conditional rendering ka matlab hai kisi condition (shart) ke mutabiq UI 
//(user interface) mein elements ko dikhana ya chhupana.

function App(){
  const  isLogin=true
  if(isLogin){
    return <h1>welcome</h1>
  }
  return  <h1>please login</h1>
}
export default  App


<--------------> example 3: <------------------------>
Ternary operator ek shortcut hai jo if-else ki jagah ek single line mein condition check karne ke liye istemal
 hota hai (Syntax: condition ? true_value : false_value).

Syntax : condition ? truepart : falsepart

function App(){
 const islogin=true
 return(
  <>
  {islogin ? <h1>welcome</h1> : <h2>please Login</h2>}
  </>
 )
}
export default  App


<-------------------> //method 3 Logical AND (&&) <------------------->
&& (AND) operator ka matlab hai ke agar pehli condition true ho, sirf
 tabhi agla element ya code render (chalao) hoga.

 function App(){
 const islogin=true
 return(
  <>
  {islogin && <p>have notify</p>}
  </>
 )
}
export default  App


<--------> render Array list <--------->
function App(){
  const fruits=['apple','banana','mango']
  return(
   <ul>
    {fruits.map((fruit,index)=>(
      <li key={index}>{fruit}</li>
    ))}
   </ul>
  )
}
export default App

<---------> complete example of list and operator and map <--------->
function App(){
  const students=['ali','ahmad','sara']
  const isTeacher=false
  return(
  <>
  <h1>Reactt class</h1>
  {isTeacher && <p>Teacher Mode</p>}
  <ul>
    {students.map((student,index)=>(
      <li key={index}>{student}</li>
    ))}
  </ul>
  </>
  )
}
export default App


<---------- >map operator <----------->
.map() array ke har item ko loop karke naya array banata hai, aur isme JSX render karne ke liye round brackets () 
aur logic likhne ke liye curly braces {} use hote hain.


